xnu 0099: the dump's term list is comma separated

mondriandumpmatch=SMP,CRASH,CODE,memorystatus parsed as "SMP", "SN", "DE"
and "morystatus": the splitter restored each separator after recording the
term (so the term still carried the rest of the list) and then advanced by the
term length again. Keep the NUL in place and step over the separator only.
The dump then prints one counter, first line and last line per term.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 020381a..727f376 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1298,11 +1298,8 @@ mondrian_log_dump(uint32_t lines)
 		size_t len = end ? (size_t)(end - t) : strlen(t);
 
 		if (len > 0) {
-			char save = t[len];
-
-			t[len] = 0;
+			t[len] = 0;             /* the separator stays NUL */
 			term[nterms++] = t;
-			t[len] = save;
 		}
 		t = end ? end + 1 : t + len;
 	}
